    "Upright needs Accessibility access to change scrolling. Until you allow it, scrolling works as usual." : {

    },
    "Upright needs Accessibility access to send keyboard shortcuts, media keys and clicks for your mouse buttons. It doesn't read what you type." : {

    },
    "Upright never reads what you type. It only listens to the HID++ channel of Logitech receivers and supported Logitech mice, and only posts the actions you assign." : {

    },
    "Upright only uses temporary button diversion, so nothing is written to the mouse’s memory. Turning the mouse off and on always restores its factory behavior." : {

    },
    "Upright sends keyboard shortcuts, media keys and clicks on behalf of your mouse. Until you allow it, mapped buttons keep their normal behavior." : {

    },
    "Upright talks to your mouse with the publicly documented HID++ 2.0 protocol, using temporary button diversion from the REPROG_CONTROLS_V4 feature (0x1B04). It does not include or depend on any Logitech software." : {

